class.description:
[VideoShadowSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"video_shadow"[/code]: it stores the directional shadow map ([method RenderingServer.directional_shadow_atlas_set_size]), the positional shadow atlas of omni and spot lights ([member Viewport.positional_shadow_atlas_size], [member Viewport.positional_shadow_atlas_16_bits], [member Viewport.positional_shadow_atlas_quad_0] to [member Viewport.positional_shadow_atlas_quad_3]) and the soft shadow filter quality ([method RenderingServer.directional_soft_shadow_filter_set_quality], [method RenderingServer.positional_soft_shadow_filter_set_quality]) for the player. Every value takes effect at once. The settings resource is a [VideoShadowSettings]; the file is [code]user://settings/video_shadow.ini[/code] by default, in the format of [member ProjectSettings.settings/storage/format].
When the game starts, the stored values are applied in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SCENE], after the root viewport exists and before the main scene is loaded. Values set earlier wait until then. The defaults are the project settings ([member ProjectSettings.rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/size], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/16_bits], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/soft_shadow_filter_quality], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/lights_and_shadows/positional_shadow/atlas_size], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/lights_and_shadows/positional_shadow/atlas_16_bits], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/lights_and_shadows/positional_shadow/atlas_quadrant_0_subdiv] to [member ProjectSettings.rendering/lights_and_shadows/positional_shadow/atlas_quadrant_3_subdiv], [member ProjectSettings.rendering/lights_and_shadows/positional_shadow/soft_shadow_filter_quality]), with their feature overrides such as [code].mobile[/code].
[b]Further viewports:[/b] the positional atlas values also go to the viewports added with [method add_viewport] and to every [Viewport] in the group [method get_viewport_group], for example a [SubViewport] that renders the 3D world. The directional shadow map and both filter qualities are global.
[b]Atlas sizes:[/b] rounded up to a power of two, like the renderers do, so the stored value is the size the atlas gets. Values out of range are clamped to [code]256[/code] to [code]16384[/code] with a warning; [code]positional_shadow_atlas_size[/code] also accepts [code]0[/code], which disables positional shadows. An enum value out of range is replaced by the default. Changing a size or a bit depth reallocates the atlas on the next frame that draws shadows (a short hitch); setting the same value again costs nothing.
[b]Renderers:[/b] Forward+, Mobile and Compatibility (default in the Web export) use every value, so [method get_unsupported_setting_names] is empty. The Compatibility renderer has three filter levels only (see [member VideoShadowSettings.directional_soft_shadow_filter_quality]).
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	$ShadowSize.value = VideoShadowSettingsServer.get_directional_shadow_atlas_size()
	$ShadowQuality.selected = VideoShadowSettingsServer.get_directional_soft_shadow_filter_quality()

func _on_shadow_size_value_changed(value):
	VideoShadowSettingsServer.set_directional_shadow_atlas_size(int(value))
	VideoShadowSettingsServer.set_positional_shadow_atlas_size(int(value))

func _on_shadow_quality_item_selected(index):
	VideoShadowSettingsServer.set_directional_soft_shadow_filter_quality(index as RenderingServer.ShadowQuality)
	VideoShadowSettingsServer.set_positional_soft_shadow_filter_quality(index as RenderingServer.ShadowQuality)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    GetNode<SpinBox>("ShadowSize").Value = VideoShadowSettingsServer.GetDirectionalShadowAtlasSize();
    GetNode<OptionButton>("ShadowQuality").Selected = (int)VideoShadowSettingsServer.GetDirectionalSoftShadowFilterQuality();
}

private void OnShadowQualityItemSelected(long index)
{
    VideoShadowSettingsServer.SetDirectionalSoftShadowFilterQuality((RenderingServer.ShadowQuality)index);
    VideoShadowSettingsServer.SetPositionalSoftShadowFilterQuality((RenderingServer.ShadowQuality)index);
    // Methods of the base class are called through Singleton.
    VideoShadowSettingsServer.Singleton.Save();
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] In C#, the static class [code skip-lint]VideoShadowSettingsServer[/code] only has the methods of this class. The methods of [SettingsServer] are called through [code]VideoShadowSettingsServer.Singleton[/code].
[b]Note:[/b] A game that sets these properties on the root viewport itself overwrites the player's values until they are applied again. Shadow settings per light (distance, splits) belong to the scene and are not part of this domain. The domain is never applied to the editor itself.
